, flatbed, expedited, and cross-border services. The LTL segment provides regional direct service and serves its customers' national transportation needs by utilizing key partner carriers for coverage areas outside of its network. The Logistics segment provides brokerage and other freight management services utilizing third-party transportation providers and equipment. The Intermodal segment offers transportation services, including arranging the movement of customers' freight through third-party intermodal rail services on its trailing equipment; and drayage services to transport loads between the railheads and customer locations. The company also provides repair and maintenance shop services, equipment leasing, warranty services, and insurance; and trailer parts manufacturing, warehousing, and certain driving academy activities. It serves retail, food and beverage, consumer and paper products, transportation and logistics, housing and building, automotive, and manufacturing industries. The company was incorporated in 1989 and is headquartered in Phoenix, Arizona.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Adam W. Miller CPA | CEO & Director | Age 44 | Compensation: $1.8M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 37K people. Revenue per employee of $201K ranks in the bottom quartile among Industrials peers, with revenue growing 6%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $34K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $770 per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 9\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Knight-Swift Transportation Hol is a large-cap industrials business with a $10.4B market cap on $7.5B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +0% over the past three years and +6% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 3% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $1.3B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 17 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 19.21\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.5\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and thin 1.3\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 1.1%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 2.9% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.3\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 8.6% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Heavy insider selling (net $16.2M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-16183489.69},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 6% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 52% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","21 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"(KNX) Movement Within Algorithmic Entry Frameworks","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/24/KNX_Movement_Within_Algorithmic_Entry_Frameworks_111226063801_1794483481.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794483481.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Knight-Swift Transportation Holdings Inc. $KNX Shares Acquired by Retirement Systems of Alabama","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/12/knight-swift-transportation-holdings-inc-knx-shares-acquired-by-retirement-systems-of-alabama.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794478669.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.9,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["m_and_a"]},{"title":"Here's Why Knight-Swift Transportation Holdings (KNX) is a Strong Value Stock","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3026363/here-s-why-knight-swift-transportation-holdings-knx-is-a-strong-value-stock?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Czacks_education_value_score-3026363","date":"2026-11-09","timestamp":1794231603.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.691,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"9,041 Knight-Swift Transportation Holdings Inc. $KNX Shares Bought by Vise Technologies Inc.","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/09/9041-knight-swift-transportation-holdings-inc-knx-shares-bought-by-vise-technologies-inc.html","date":"2026-